sequenceDiagram
    participant B as Browser
    participant NA as notify-api
    participant DB as db-service
    participant WS as ws-service

    Note over B,WS: Connections are reused, none opened per request<br/>notify-api keeps one shared HTTP client (keep-alive) to db-service and ws-service<br/>db-service opens its Postgres pool (10 connections) once at startup

    B->>NA: POST /notify
    activate NA
    NA->>DB: POST /write
    activate DB
    Note right of DB: borrow a pooled connection,<br/>INSERT, give it back<br/>(waits if all 10 are busy)
    DB-->>NA: 200 OK (row inserted)
    deactivate DB
    NA->>WS: POST /push
    activate WS
    WS-->>B: WebSocket message (delivered)
    WS-->>NA: 200 OK
    deactivate WS
    NA-->>B: 200 OK (whole chain done)
    deactivate NA
